Rule 3 (if bins is a list of integers, its length must equal the number of dimensions of sample, and all elements must be positive)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : list(int)} |= ndim(v_1) = 2 ∧ v_2.len = shape(v_1, 1) ∧ ∀i ∈ [0, v_2.len - 1] : v_2[i] > 0
>>
Rule 4 (if bins is a tuple of integers, its length must equal the number of dimensions of sample, and all elements must be positive)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tuple(int)} |= ndim(v_1) = 2 ∧ v_2.len = shape(v_1, 1) ∧ ∀i ∈ [0, v_2.len - 1] : v_2[i] > 0
>>
Rule 5 (if bins is an integer, it must be greater than 0)
{v_1 : int} |= v_1 > 0
