Rule 11 (if sample and weights are both tensors, they must have matching datatypes, and sample should be a floating-point type)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= ndim(v_1) = 2 ∧ ndim(v_2) = 1 ∧ 6 ≤ dtype_(v_1) ∧ dtype_(v_1) ≤ 8 ∧ dtype_(v_1) = dtype_(v_2)
>>
Rule 12 (when bins is specified as a 1D tensor, its length must equal the number of dimensions of the sample, and its dtype must be integer)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= ndim(v_1) = 2 ∧ ndim(v_2) = 1 ∧ shape(v_2, 0) = shape(v_1, 1) ∧ 1 ≤ dtype_(v_2) ∧ dtype_(v_2) ≤ 5
>>
Rule 13 (weights must be a 1D numeric tensor of integer or float type, with length matching the number of samples)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= ndim(v_1) = 2 ∧ ndim(v_2) = 1 ∧ shape(v_1, 0) = shape(v_2, 0) ∧ 1 ≤ dtype_(v_2) ∧ dtype_(v_2) ≤ 8
>>
Rule 14 (if both bins and range are specified as lists, their lengths must be equal)
{v_1 : list(int), v_2 : list(tuple(float))} |= v_1.len = v_2.len
>>
Rule 15 (if both bins and range are specified as tuples, their lengths must be equal)
{v_1 : tuple(int), v_2 : tuple(tuple(float))} |= v_1.len = v_2.len
